cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this environment, the trained models, or the GUI in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Splendor: a fast PufferLib environment with league self-play, Elo and MCTS"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Aditya
    email: adityaku@andrew.cmu.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sylindril/splendor"
url: "https://github.com/Sylindril/splendor"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - Splendor
  - PufferLib
  - self-play
  - MCTS
abstract: >-
  An exact-rules, 2-4 player Splendor board game environment written in C for
  PufferLib (about 4 million turns per second per core), with masked MLP
  policies, a prioritized fictitious self-play league trainer, a Bradley-Terry
  Elo ladder, batched PUCT Monte Carlo tree search with an AlphaZero-style
  training loop, shipped trained models, and a browser GUI for watching or
  playing against the agents.
